          %h3#general General
          %p The original article is
          %ul
            %li#Albert
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abraham+Adrian+Albert"}> Abraham Adrian Albert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On a Certain Algebra of Quantum Mechanics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2307/1968118"} 10.2307/1968118
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1968118"} JSTOR
          %p A textbook account is in
          %ul
            %li#SpringerVeltkamp00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tonny+Springer"}> Tonny Springer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ferdinand+Veldkamp"} Ferdinand Veldkamp
              = succeed "," do
                %em Octonions, Jordan Algebras, and Exceptional Groups
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li#Baez02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/octonions/node12.html"} section 3.4
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕆
                        %msup
